{"n": 69, "w": 1600, "h": 1243, "img": "69.webp", "text": "6216-0 ACTIVE CHECK CONTROL\n\nee Se nnn ne\n\nACTIVE CHECK CONTROL\n\n1. When the Ignition Switch is initially\nplaced in “Run,” the Active Check\nControf Arm Indicator flashes, and\nthe Active Check Control Unit Brake\nLight LED and panel light illuminate\nfor test purposes, Depressing the brake\npedal clears the display.\n\n2. When the Ignition Switch is placed\nin “Run,” fault monitoring begins.\nTo monitor the low beams, rear lights,\nor license lights, those circuits must be\non. The brake lights are monitered only\nwhile the brake pedal is depressed. An\nexception to this is when all brake light\ncircuits are open. A fault will be indicated\nwith the Ignition Switch in Run.\n\n3. When a fault occurs, the alarm indicator\nflashes, the appropriate LED fault indi-\neator lights, and the panel light goes on\nfor five seconds. Depressing the test\nbutton will clear the alarm indicator,\nbut the LED fault indicator remains an.\n\n4, To test the unit, depress the test\nbutton. The LED fault indicators\nand the panel lights should go on.\n\nENGINE OL\n\nHOT IN ACCY. RUN OR START\nrorer rm ===\" POWER\n\n18 1.5 VI/GY FUSE\nDETAILS\n\nACTIVE CHECK CONTROL UNIT\n\nnom sea, 1\nKY\n\n‘SOLIDSTATE ‘FAULTINDIGATOR\n\n22 21\n\nPOWER\n.5 YL/BK SYL DISTRIBUTION\n\n| cowry\n\"DISTRIBUTION\n\nAUXILIARY\n\n1 ¥L/BU\n\nGROUND |\nDISTRIBUTION HEADLIGHTS\n2", "words": [["6216-0", 0.0521, 0.0352, 0.1135, 0.0526], ["ACTIVE", 0.1329, 0.0348, 0.1991, 0.0519], ["CHECK", 0.2044, 0.0341, 0.2653, 0.0515], ["CONTROL", 0.2706, 0.0329, 0.3565, 0.0507], ["ee", 0.0503, 0.0556, 0.1756, 0.0704], ["Se", 0.2929, 0.0556, 0.3638, 0.0704], ["nnn", 0.4335, 0.0556, 0.8294, 0.0704], ["ne", 0.8962, 0.0556, 0.9394, 0.0704], ["ACTIVE", 0.1924, 0.1847, 0.2453, 0.1983], ["CHECK", 0.2497, 0.1836, 0.2979, 0.198], ["CONTROL", 0.3024, 0.1828, 0.3709, 0.1972], ["1.", 0.2121, 0.2222, 0.2176, 0.2309], ["When", 0.22, 0.2218, 0.2379, 0.2305], ["the", 0.2406, 0.22